{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:0.4", "PA_ja_214:1.1"], "en": "4. The Puṇṇanadī Jātaka “The river they call Puṇṇa, where they say water is drinkable;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:1.2"], "en": "the barley that grows there, where they say it is hidden.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:1.3"], "en": "\"He whom they call one who has gone far away—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:1.4"], "en": "come now, O Brahmin, enjoy this gift from him.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:2.1"], "en": "\"Since the king remembers me...\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:2.2"], "en": "Even a crow should be driven away;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:2.3", "PA_ja_214:2.4"], "en": "for swans, cranes, and peacocks are far superior to one who is unchaste.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_214:3.1"], "en": "The Puṇṇanadī Jātaka, the fourth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
]
